{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nS2 makes runtime parsing and committed package help share one argparse source, but downstream consumers can still recreate drift. Today `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` regex-parses the intercept ladder and owns a curated command table; help/exit-code tests rebuild route sets; clean-wheel CI does not exercise every parser-derived artifact or lazy-reference contract.\n\n## Approach\nMake registries and S2-generated parser artifacts the only enumerable syntax inputs for documentation and distribution checks.\n\n- Generate every command syntax/options section in `docs/cli-reference.md` from registry enumeration plus the exact committed package-help bytes proven current by `scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check`.\n- Delete `INTERCEPT_COMMANDS`, source regex parsing, and any hand-maintained command/usage/option census.\n- Keep cross-command rationale and examples editorial, but structurally separate from generated syntax sections. A deterministic lint rejects editorial `Usage:`/option-table authorities and validates referenced top-level spellings against the route registry; parser artifacts remain authoritative on disagreement.\n- Replace manual route unions in overview/help/argparse/exit-code tests with canonical/exact/compatibility/hidden/retired registry enumeration.\n- Extend the local-capable optionality harness and `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml` clean-wheel lane to build a no-extras wheel, run `gen_cli_help.py --check` and `gen_cli_reference.py --check`, render every approved help form in a fresh directory, and assert no operation/config/store/handler/heavy import.\n- Add a full-runtime-extra contract that resolves every lazy handler/parser/selector reference and validates every capability-to-extra mapping without executing command logic.\n- Smoke-test `rebar-mcp` separately. Every CI check must have the same repository-local command for non-GitHub environments.\n\nRegistry validation covers route/resource census. S2's generator covers parser/artifact drift. Full-extra validation covers lazy-reference typos. No source grep substitutes for observable help/dispatch behavior.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nDerived compatibility exports remain through S6. Reference syntax changes only with reviewed parser/generated-help changes; editorial prose may improve without redefining grammar. Reverting docs/generator/test/CI changes leaves runtime and stored data untouched.\n\n## Testing\nUse byte regeneration checks, generator unit tests, real clean-wheel subprocesses, import blockers, and full-extra symbol resolution. Negative fixtures include a parser/help byte drift, unresolved parser/handler, stray resource, omitted route, hidden alias leakage, retired token, editorial syntax table, unknown prose spelling, and heavy optional import. Prove each test collects and executes under a gating local/CI command.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check` and `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` prove the complete reference syntax/options derive from runtime-used parser artifacts and are byte-current.\n- [ ] No source regex, `INTERCEPT_COMMANDS`, manual command-description census, or editorial usage/option table remains.\n- [ ] Overview/help/exit-code tests enumerate all route classes from the registry rather than reconstructing policy sets.\n- [ ] A clean no-extras wheel renders every approved help form with exact bytes and no operation/config/store/parser/handler/heavy-import effect.\n- [ ] The full-extra contract resolves every handler/parser/selector and capability-to-extra reference without command execution.\n- [ ] Editorial examples/rationale are structurally separate, registry-linted for top-level spellings, and never override generated syntax.\n- [ ] The same commands run locally and in portable CI, with `rebar-mcp` tested as a separate entry point."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787070777808809001,"uuid":"c3cacb79-adfe-4b76-9fd5-94818a54f311"}